From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 add the PCK-600 power controller

Adds the pck600 power-controller node so DT consumers can reference
power-domains = <&pck600 PD_...>. The immediate need is the USB3/dwc3 node
(PD_USB2), which is wired by a later USB3 patch (arm64-dts-a733-usb3-power-domain), not here.

reg 0x07060000 size 0xb000 = 11 domains * 0x1000, matching silicon
(/proc/iomem: 07060000-0706afff : power-controller@7060000) and the ARM-view
memory map (PPU @0x07060000). No clock or reset is wired: the A733 driver
variant (patch `pmdomain-sunxi-pck600-add-a733-support`) is attach-only and holds the boot power state; the block
is already clocked and out of reset by boot firmware (its USB2 domain is
boot-on).

Placed next to the GIC in the minimal DT (the r-domain nodes r_ccu /
rtc_ccu are only added later, with USB). Node only, no consumer
references.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -157,6 +157,18 @@
 			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * PCK-600 power controller (Arm CoreLink PCK-600 / PPU). Provides
+		 * the SoC power domains; PD_USB2 (index 8) is boot-on (on silicon,
+		 * the 8 GiB board: status @0x07068008 = 0x8). Attach-only driver variant
+		 * (patch `pmdomain-sunxi-pck600-add-a733-support`): no clock/reset wired, block is boot-clocked.
+		 */
+		pck600: power-controller@7060000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07060000 0x0 0xb000>;
+			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		uart0: serial@2500000 {
 			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
 			reg = <0x0 0x02500000 0x0 0x400>;
